  "limitations": [
    "Historical era x housing-keyword poststratification estimates routes, not confirmed housing truth; retained includes uncertain scope.",
    "Large groups use pooled routing. Routing sensitivity changes one observation per cell; not a confidence interval.",
    "First-pass input scales by source characters; output and reasoning scale by groups. Fixed review prefix scales by groups, remaining input by characters.",
    "Repair calibration is 14 purposively selected retained groups and only 2 exclusions; difficult cases may overstate average repair output.",
    "Joint repair is an exploratory estimate from one six-retained-group batch. It assumes six cases fit together; larger groups need smaller batches or individual review. Use individual-review projections as a planning alternative, not a guaranteed ceiling.",
    "Duration bounds, when present, are calibrated on six difficult retained groups, with no assumed input caching. Output scales by group, input by archive source characters. This is a rough incremental estimate, not a representative population sample.",
    "Repair assumes a warm 4992-token prefix only, with no cross-pass source cache credit. First pass uses observed cache fractions; no-cache totals also provided.",
    "Reasoning tokens are part of output, never added a second time. No retry allowance in base projections; reserve 25% for operational variation.",
    "Four groups above 400000 characters require a separately designed route and are excluded, not silently truncated.",
    "Estimates describe a fresh full run, not incremental cost after reusing existing results. Prices are project-configured DeepSeek Flash non-peak rates."
  ]
